/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# bench artifacts (fixtures are fetched, not committed)
/bench/fixtures/repos
/bench/fixtures/artifacts
*.stats.json
*.js.map

# bench/results/ is deliberately NOT ignored. Those files are the evidence
# trail: every number in the docs cites one, and a measurement nobody can
# inspect is a claim. They are a few KB each because the raw fixtures are not
# committed - the results record the fixture's parameters, not its bytes.

# local caches
.nopeat-cache/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
dist/
report*.html
*-report.html

# mdbook site: sources (docs/) and build output stay out of version control.
book/

# webpack-bundle-analyzer's raw json export: written by every parity run, and it is
# the reference tool's output, not a record of ours.
bench/results/parity-wba.json

# The prose under docs/ is not published. `docs/assets/` and `docs/schema/` are,
# and a bare `docs/` would take both with it: the README embeds six figures from
# the first and links four contract files in the second, so ignoring the whole
# tree ships a front page with broken images and dead links.
docs/*
!docs/assets/
!docs/schema/

history-rewrite-report.md
aiscan_tmp.py

# Not published: the curated issue list, which is a working document rather than
# a document anyone reads. It is gitignored rather than deleted because it is
# kept up to date and pushed to GitHub by hand once it is ready.
docs/good-first-issues.md
